    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 215,
        "text": "Hi everyone, thanks for coming to the student council meeting. Today we need to plan our class debate. The topic is: should school start later in the morning? I think we should start with clear topic sentences.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7495e17e19c0acba3ba70173dc7235cda8ec821c38acbf21cb884157cfca899e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 222,
        "sourceEnd": 501,
        "text": "Good idea. So, each speaker needs a topic sentence that states their main point. Then they support it with reasons and examples. For example, a topic sentence could be: 'Starting school later improves students' health.' Then the speaker gives evidence, like research about sleep.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "60147a9f379621ceebc57070954353b022dbaa871bcfd69d8a8b34eb6d0e95ef",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 508,
        "sourceEnd": 728,
        "text": "Right. Although some students like early starts, many feel tired in first period. While the school says early starts prepare us for work, students say they can't concentrate. Because of this, we want to debate the issue.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "89ab9dab1ca5507076b9fe13c59aabecc1701a1c4ffd749ee15d639cb2d7c379",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 735,
        "sourceEnd": 947,
        "text": "Also, we need to use 'because' and 'because of' correctly. 'Because' is followed by a clause, like 'because students need more sleep.' 'Because of' is followed by a noun phrase, like 'because of the early start.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3c3a3a26c5f52512f733b9e389342b8f0612486b0f1c695af0986edb3e24aa1b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 954,
        "sourceEnd": 1178,
        "text": "Exactly. And we should also use 'although' and 'while' to show contrast. For instance: 'Although the school day is long, students can still do sports after school.' Or 'While some teachers prefer early starts, others don't.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "be69153f7afdfe7e5876da3ba0359a2b4c87e6c0f89facbb16b9084f1023ff4f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1185,
        "sourceEnd": 1423,
        "text": "Let's also think about the structure of our arguments. Each paragraph should have a topic sentence, supporting sentences, and a concluding sentence. The topic sentence is like a signpost. It tells the listener what the paragraph is about.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "4f34848ce24402f222dc42c908029165dd6c4dd389fb351f12e61c1df91891ae",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1430,
        "sourceEnd": 1582,
        "text": "Yes. And we must avoid going off-topic. So, when we prepare our speeches, we should check that every supporting sentence connects to the topic sentence.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "cf865a7dadfa76dc54029db873183c090758b1ce24e7d34c7f6d70eb2a6e2136",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1589,
        "sourceEnd": 1776,
        "text": "Another thing: we need to anticipate counterarguments. For example, if we argue for later starts, we should also mention the opposing view and refute it. That makes our argument stronger.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "0b41284a3cb29eddf45c252f1a79b14251c10b9252cd08d7bf4d7f5df0eb284c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1783,
        "sourceEnd": 1987,
        "text": "Good point. So, in the debate, we'll have two teams: one for later starts, one against. Each team will present their arguments using topic sentences and supporting sentences. Then we'll have a discussion.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "eb048d1a001d1de8edb6c9e9ee33bb0d2176921a3b2d930e0c65952f800ea1ec",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1994,
        "sourceEnd": 2109,
        "text": "And remember, the debate is next Friday at 3 p.m. in the school hall. We need to prepare our speeches by Wednesday.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a15db3f04a032ff2c07207d435d20528f0a0682cba429dc6997d070b3cddf66e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2116,
        "sourceEnd": 2156,
        "text": "OK, let's get started. Thanks, everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "ba981cee0b176360f6c0c6499093f1f8facf98c571e6d81732b88f6eb0819fe3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
